<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-08T21:09:35+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:09:35 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Ohio homeowner ordered to pay contractor $45,806 despite cosmetic defects in basement walls]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135661039.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Ohio homeowner was ordered to pay a contractor $45,806 for a concrete foundation with cosmetic flaws. The court found that structural integrity was maintained, despite visible surface defects. The homeowner had initially refused payment, claiming that the imperfections reduced property value. The appeals court upheld the lower court decision, emphasizing the importance of structural safety over cosmetic issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-homeowner-refused-to-pay-for-basement-walls-after-spotting-defects-in-a-2021-project-judges-said-the-foundation-was-structurally-sound-despite-cosmetic-flaws-and-upheld-a-45806-payment-to-the-contractor/articleshow/135661039.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-homeowner-refused-to-pay-for-basement-walls-after-spotting-defects-in-a-2021-project-judges-said-the-foundation-was-structurally-sound-despite-cosmetic-flaws-and-upheld-a-45806-payment-to-the-contractor/articleshow/135661039.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T20:52:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135661589,imgsize-151106.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump says US took ‘giant step back in history’ after Democrats’ midterm victory]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135661310.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/giant-step-back-in-history-trump-blames-democrats-midterm-sweep-for-3-trillion-market-loss/articleshow/135661310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/giant-step-back-in-history-trump-blames-democrats-midterm-sweep-for-3-trillion-market-loss/articleshow/135661310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T20:45:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135661389,imgsize-56432.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[North Dakota woman loses $110,000 home improvement claim after breakup with partner]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135660646.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After her relationship concluded, Mary Roth pursued the return of over $110,000 she invested in home enhancements. However, the North Dakota Supreme Court determined that she could not secure restitution through an unjust enrichment claim. The ruling underscored that Roth needed to demonstrate an actual financial benefit to the property owner, something her receipts failed to do when it came to increasing the property's market value.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-dakota-woman-spent-more-than-110000-on-purchases-for-a-house-she-built-with-her-partner-on-land-held-by-his-family-trust-after-they-split-a-court-rejected-her-claim-for-the-homes-improvements/articleshow/135660646.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-dakota-woman-spent-more-than-110000-on-purchases-for-a-house-she-built-with-her-partner-on-land-held-by-his-family-trust-after-they-split-a-court-rejected-her-claim-for-the-homes-improvements/articleshow/135660646.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T20:02:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135661015,imgsize-228339.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egypt train collision: Several injured as train derails after hitting another train]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135660889.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egypt-train-collision-over-60-injured-as-passenger-train-derails-after-hitting-another-train-in-giza/articleshow/135660889.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egypt-train-collision-over-60-injured-as-passenger-train-derails-after-hitting-another-train-in-giza/articleshow/135660889.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:59:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135660971,imgsize-192572.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[West Virginia court overturns $31,054 home value payout but protects wife's mortgage share]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135660392.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The West Virginia Supreme Court of Appeals has overturned a previous decision regarding a premarital home. The court ruled that the husband is not liable for the home's market value increase during marriage. This ruling clarifies how separate property and marital contributions are treated in divorce cases. However, the former wife is entitled to financial interest from mortgage principal payments made during the marriage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/west-virginia-supreme-court-reverses-31054-divorce-payout-tied-to-rise-in-value-of-house-bought-before-marriage-wife-remains-entitled-to-a-share-of-mortgage-principal-reduction/articleshow/135660392.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/west-virginia-supreme-court-reverses-31054-divorce-payout-tied-to-rise-in-value-of-house-bought-before-marriage-wife-remains-entitled-to-a-share-of-mortgage-principal-reduction/articleshow/135660392.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:30:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135660537,imgsize-123465.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Far-right wingnuts storm Diwali fest in Seattle after lights go out on MAGA]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135660200.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/far-right-wingnuts-storm-diwali-fest-in-seattle-after-lights-go-out-on-maga/articleshow/135660200.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/far-right-wingnuts-storm-diwali-fest-in-seattle-after-lights-go-out-on-maga/articleshow/135660200.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:16:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chidanand Rajghatta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135660327,imgsize-969224.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Queen Elizabeth II’s final days at Balmoral Castle: Inside her 53,000-acre Scottish sanctuary]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135630670.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Queen Elizabeth II spent her final days at Balmoral Castle, her beloved Scottish retreat spanning 53,000 acres. The royal estate held decades of cherished family memories, offering her peace and comfort amid nature. From royal summer holidays to her final moments, discover why Balmoral remained one of the Queen’s most treasured places throughout her life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/queen-elizabeth-iis-final-days-at-balmoral-castle-inside-the-53000-acre-scottish-estate-where-she-found-peace-made-cherished-family-memories-and-spent-her-last-moments-surrounded-by-nature-and-loved-ones/articleshow/135630670.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/queen-elizabeth-iis-final-days-at-balmoral-castle-inside-the-53000-acre-scottish-estate-where-she-found-peace-made-cherished-family-memories-and-spent-her-last-moments-surrounded-by-nature-and-loved-ones/articleshow/135630670.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135631787,imgsize-133654.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A €20 flea-market lamp sells for €251,000 after hidden signature is discovered]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135630119.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/a-woman-bought-an-unremarkable-black-lamp-for-just-20-at-a-french-flea-market-her-daughter-spotted-a-hidden-signature-and-the-rediscovered-ceramic-piece-sold-for-251000/articleshow/135630119.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/a-woman-bought-an-unremarkable-black-lamp-for-just-20-at-a-french-flea-market-her-daughter-spotted-a-hidden-signature-and-the-rediscovered-ceramic-piece-sold-for-251000/articleshow/135630119.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:54:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135630305,imgsize-478716.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rare Altdorfer landscape hidden for 70 years after 1957 acquisition could fetch £5 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135629526.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An undiscovered masterpiece by Albrecht Altdorfer, the renowned German Renaissance painter, is set to hit the auction block at Sotheby's this December. This exquisite work, featuring a stunning forest scene crowned by a rainbow, has been held privately since 1957. With Altdorfer's oil landscapes being incredibly scarce, this auction represents a rare chance for collectors, the first of its kind since 1980, including viewings in New York and London beforehand.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-renaissance-landscape-acquired-by-a-swiss-collectors-father-in-1957-vanished-from-public-view-for-nearly-70-years-experts-have-identified-it-as-a-rare-altdorfer-worth-up-to-5-million/articleshow/135629526.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-renaissance-landscape-acquired-by-a-swiss-collectors-father-in-1957-vanished-from-public-view-for-nearly-70-years-experts-have-identified-it-as-a-rare-altdorfer-worth-up-to-5-million/articleshow/135629526.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135629712,imgsize-2268237.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[North Dakota court bars unmarried couples from jointly adopting children, despite parental consent]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135659977.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a landmark decision, North Dakota’s Supreme Court ruled that unmarried couples are barred from adopting a child together, as dictated by existing state law. This case involved a grandmother and her partner who intended to adopt her grandchild, with agreement from both biological parents. The court clarified that only legislative changes can alter adoption laws, while allowing individual adoption requests from either of the parties involved.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-dakota-grandmother-and-her-longtime-partner-cared-for-her-grandson-from-the-age-of-four-months-and-both-parents-consented-to-adoption-the-state-supreme-court-says-the-unmarried-couple-cannot-adopt-jointly/articleshow/135659977.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-dakota-grandmother-and-her-longtime-partner-cared-for-her-grandson-from-the-age-of-four-months-and-both-parents-consented-to-adoption-the-state-supreme-court-says-the-unmarried-couple-cannot-adopt-jointly/articleshow/135659977.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:10:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135660194,imgsize-222717.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida appeals court orders fresh review after wife loses alimony and all parenting time following pay cut]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135612084.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an emerging divorce case from Florida, the Fourth District Court has called for a deeper examination of the rulings made by the Broward County trial court involving Rebecca Zalkin and Jeffrey Zalkin. The initial decision denied alimony and granted sole parental responsibility to the husband without sufficient reasoning. The appellate court highlighted the necessity for validated income data and adherence to legal protocol.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-a-florida-woman-reduced-her-teaching-pay-from-about-49450-to-20000-her-divorce-court-denied-alimony-and-gave-her-husband-all-parenting-time-an-appeals-court-ordered-a-fresh-review-of-support-and-parenting/articleshow/135612084.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-a-florida-woman-reduced-her-teaching-pay-from-about-49450-to-20000-her-divorce-court-denied-alimony-and-gave-her-husband-all-parenting-time-an-appeals-court-ordered-a-fresh-review-of-support-and-parenting/articleshow/135612084.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:04:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135612186,imgsize-101859.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Hometown Cha-Cha-Cha' actress Shin Min-a quietly donated over $2.7 million in 15 years to help burn victims, underprivileged children and vulnerable families]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135629053.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Since 2009, South Korean actress Shin Min-a has made a remarkable impact through her charitable donations, amounting to more than 3.7 billion won for various causes. Focusing on aiding burn victims, disadvantaged youth, and disaster-affected areas, her annual contributions of 100 million won reported by the Hallym Burn Foundation could total 1.1 billion won by 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/hometown-cha-cha-cha-actress-shin-min-a-quietly-donated-over-2-7-million-in-15-years-to-help-burn-victims-underprivileged-children-and-vulnerable-families-charity-officials-initially-mistook-her-recurring-contributions-for-an-error/articleshow/135629053.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/hometown-cha-cha-cha-actress-shin-min-a-quietly-donated-over-2-7-million-in-15-years-to-help-burn-victims-underprivileged-children-and-vulnerable-families-charity-officials-initially-mistook-her-recurring-contributions-for-an-error/articleshow/135629053.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T19:04:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135629207,imgsize-740031.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia reverses military land sale plans after protests, saving four historic sites]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135659211.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Australian government has opted to retain four significant historical military sites in public hands, responding to widespread public dissent against their potential sale. Notably, Victoria Barracks in Sydney and other sites in Victoria will remain untouched. The government aims to find new public purposes for these locations while preserving their heritage, and part of the broader reforms includes returning certain military lands to Indigenous communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-planned-to-sell-67-military-sites-to-raise-1-8-billion-but-public-protests-over-sydneys-166-year-old-victoria-barracks-prompted-a-november-8-reversal-that-will-keep-four-historic-sites-publicly-owned/articleshow/135659211.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-planned-to-sell-67-military-sites-to-raise-1-8-billion-but-public-protests-over-sydneys-166-year-old-victoria-barracks-prompted-a-november-8-reversal-that-will-keep-four-historic-sites-publicly-owned/articleshow/135659211.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T18:51:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135659968,imgsize-243876.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At least 21 dead after migrant boat sinks off Senegal's northwestern coast]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135659201.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-21-dead-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegals-northwestern-coast/articleshow/135659201.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-21-dead-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegals-northwestern-coast/articleshow/135659201.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T18:16:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135659273,imgsize-215186.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK developer Urban Splash and four firms ordered to pay £46.5m for fire-safety repairs in Manchester]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135657936.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The tribunal has mandated that Urban Splash and its related entities must shell out £46.5 million for crucial fire safety refurbishments across seven residential projects in Manchester. While the tribunal recognized the necessity for these repairs, it moderated the government’s original financial demand due to previous regulatory shortcomings. Housing Secretary Angela Rayner highlighted the critical need for accountability in ensuring safe living conditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-the-uk-a-developer-and-four-linked-firms-have-been-ordered-to-pay-46-5-million-towards-fire-safety-work-on-seven-manchester-buildings-following-a-landmark-tribunal-ruling-that-cut-the-governments-claim/articleshow/135657936.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-the-uk-a-developer-and-four-linked-firms-have-been-ordered-to-pay-46-5-million-towards-fire-safety-work-on-seven-manchester-buildings-following-a-landmark-tribunal-ruling-that-cut-the-governments-claim/articleshow/135657936.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T17:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135658546,imgsize-158614.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Jersey store donates $30,000 bonus after selling $847m Powerball jackpot ticket]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135658566.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On November 4, a stunning Powerball ticket purchased at Wegmans Food Market in New Jersey clinched an impressive $847 million jackpot, breaking a 35-draw drought for big winners. The lucky supermarket will earn a bonus of $30,000, which is earmarked for donation to the Community FoodBank of New Jersey. New Jersey law allows lottery winners to stay anonymous indefinitely, so don't forget to check those numbers and secure your ticket!]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-supermarket-sold-the-winning-ticket-for-an-847-million-powerball-jackpot-and-received-a-30000-retailer-bonus-instead-of-keeping-it-the-store-said-the-money-would-go-to-a-food-bank/articleshow/135658566.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-supermarket-sold-the-winning-ticket-for-an-847-million-powerball-jackpot-and-received-a-30000-retailer-bonus-instead-of-keeping-it-the-store-said-the-money-would-go-to-a-food-bank/articleshow/135658566.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T17:57:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135658858,imgsize-86450.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chicago’s World’s Fair featured a two-speed moving sidewalk carrying visitors to the Peristyle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135629843.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chicagos-1893-worlds-fair-introduced-an-unusual-attraction-a-two-speed-moving-sidewalk-that-carried-visitors-from-the-steamship-pier-to-the-peristyle-at-3-mph-or-6-mph-for-five-cents/articleshow/135629843.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chicagos-1893-worlds-fair-introduced-a